   Once the declarative documentation has been generated,
   create the Git commit.

   The Git commit message should consist of:

       1. One newly generated concise summary line.

       2. A blank line.

       3. The body of the imperative heredoc that generated
          the changes, formatted for a conventional Git
          commit message.

   Extract the body of the archived imperative heredoc,
