   The Git commit message is its human-readable companion.

   The commit should include:

       - The accepted implementation changes.
       - The archived imperative script.
       - The new or updated declarative documentation.
       - Any directly related supporting changes.

   Associate the commit with the relevant completed task.

   If multiple completed tasks are pending, handle them
